Protein Name: Lysosome-associated membrane glycoprotein 2
Organism: Homo sapiens (Human)
UniProt Accession ID: P13473
Protein Function: LAMP-2 is a lysosomal membrane protein involved in lysosome formation, maintenance of lysosomal function, and regulation of autophagy. It helps control lysosomal activity and cellular waste degradation.
Cellular Location: Lysosome membrane; also found in endosome and cell membrane.
